🏆 GOLAZO HUB — eFOOTBALL TOURNAMENT RULES
============================================================

📌 TOURNAMENT RULEBOOK
These rules apply to every participant. Our goal is simple:
keep the tournament fair, enjoyable, competitive, and transparent
for everyone.

------------------------------------------------------------
1. ⚽ MATCH FORMAT
------------------------------------------------------------

• Every Group Stage match will be played for 8 minutes.
• Injury: ON
• Substitution: 6/3
• Form: Both Normal
• Extra Time: OFF
• Penalty: OFF

• Every Group Stage match must be played using the exact format above.

• Knockout Stage:
  - Extra Time: ON
  - Penalty: ON

• Players are not allowed to change the match settings on their own.
  If there is any special situation, please contact the Admin before
  starting the match.


------------------------------------------------------------
2. ⏰ MATCH DEADLINE
------------------------------------------------------------

• Each match will have a specific Deadline.
• Both players are responsible for completing their match within
  the given Deadline.
• If a match is not completed before the Deadline, the Admin will
  review both players' activity, communication, and effort to play.
• Based on the available activity and evidence, the Admin may award
  an Auto Win.

📌 Important:
Simply saying "we could not play" will not automatically make either
player the winner. Both sides may be reviewed before a final decision
is made.

• Please contact your opponent early and make a proper plan so the
  match can be completed on time.


------------------------------------------------------------
3. 🚫 QUITTING THE TOURNAMENT
------------------------------------------------------------

• If a player decides to leave the Tournament in the middle of it,
  all of their remaining matches will be recorded as 0-1 Auto Loss.
• The results will then be submitted to the Official Website.
• A player who intentionally leaves the Tournament may also receive
  additional punishment from the Admin.
• In serious cases, an additional 3-goal penalty may be applied,
  depending on the situation and the Admin's decision.

📌 Please make sure you have enough time to complete the Tournament
before joining.


------------------------------------------------------------
4. 🚷 PROXY / PLAYING FOR SOMEONE ELSE
------------------------------------------------------------

• A player must always play their own matches.
• Asking another person to play on your behalf will be considered
  PROXY and is strictly prohibited.
• Using another player's Account/ID is also not allowed.
• Allowing someone else to play using your Account is equally prohibited.

✅ If PROXY is confirmed:
• All matches of that player in the Tournament may be given Auto Loss.
• Their Tournament results may be corrected or removed.
• The player may be BANNED from the next Tournament.
• For serious or repeated violations, the Admin may take stronger action.

📌 Screenshots, Screen Recordings, Match Records, or other reliable
evidence may be reviewed when dealing with a PROXY complaint.


------------------------------------------------------------
5. 🛡️ SQUAD RULES
------------------------------------------------------------

Each Tournament may use a specific Squad Type.

Examples:
• Authentic Squad
• Max Squad
• National Squad
• Club Squad
• Any other Squad type announced for that Tournament

Important Rules:
• Once a Tournament starts with a specific Squad Type, that same
  Squad Type must be used throughout the Tournament.
• Players cannot switch to another Squad Type in the middle of the
  Tournament.
• Playing with an unauthorized Squad may be treated as a Rule Violation.
• Depending on the situation, the Admin may change the result, award
  an Auto Loss, or apply another suitable penalty.

📌 Before starting a match, both players should make sure they are
using the correct Squad Type.


------------------------------------------------------------
6. 📊 WEBSITE PROGRESS & STATISTICS
------------------------------------------------------------

After each match, the results will be updated on the Official Website.

Players will be able to track their Tournament Performance, including:

🏆 Wins — How many matches they have won
🎮 Matches Played — How many matches they have played
⚽ Goals — How many goals they have scored
📈 Other Stats — Additional performance statistics

• The Website will help players easily follow their progress throughout
  the Tournament.
• Official results and statistics may be updated by the Admin when needed.


------------------------------------------------------------
7. 🌐 NETWORK ISSUES DURING A MATCH
------------------------------------------------------------

• If a player faces a Network Issue during a match, they should record
  their screen and keep clear evidence of the problem.
• Screen Recording or other valid proof may be required when reporting
  a Network Issue.
• Without enough evidence, the Admin may reject the complaint.
• The Admin may review both players' recordings, match situation,
  activity, and other available evidence before making a decision.
• Depending on the situation, the Admin may allow the match to continue,
  request a replay, or decide the final result.

📌 Fake complaints, false information, or misleading evidence about
Network Issues may be treated as a serious Rule Violation.

• For Network Issue disputes, the Group Admin's decision will be final.


------------------------------------------------------------
⚠️ FINAL NOTICE — FAIR PLAY
------------------------------------------------------------

Please help us keep GOLAZO HUB a fair, friendly, and competitive
Tournament.

• No PROXY or cheating.
• No fake or edited evidence.
• Respect your opponent and communicate properly.
• Follow the announced Match Format, Squad Rules, and Deadline.
• If you are unsure about any rule, ask the Admin before playing the match.

🚨 Any Rule Violation may lead to a warning, Auto Loss, result change,
ban, or another penalty depending on the situation.

👑 For all GOLAZO HUB Tournament matters, the ADMIN'S DECISION
will be considered FINAL.

